class:: EffectiveDuration
summary:: Fraction of the window occupied by significant envelope energy
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Amplitude

description::
Counts RMS frames at least 10 percent of the largest RMS value in the window, corresponding to a relative -20 dB amplitude threshold, and divides by the number of frames. Exact silence returns zero. This is a rolling duration ratio rather than an event duration in seconds.

Frames contain nonoverlapping RMS measurements. Output stays zero until a complete observation window is available, then updates once per RMS frame. Silence returns zero. Runtime cost is linear in windowTime/frameTime per update; there is no callback allocation. These descriptors are rolling summaries and do not segment individual events. Formulas are independently implemented from standard weighted moments and linear regression.

The nearest vanilla building block is link::Classes/Amplitude::, which tracks instantaneous level; this UGen summarizes its recent distribution in time.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time observation duration, 2*frameTime through 10 seconds. Rounded up to whole RMS frames.

argument:: frameTime
Initialization-time RMS frame duration, 0.001 through 0.1 seconds.

argument:: floorDB
Silence floor in dBFS, clipped to -160..0. Used by dynamic complexity and dB regression; temporal moments use the original energy.

returns::
Active fraction from zero through one.

examples::
EffectiveDuration counts the fraction of rolling RMS frames at or above 10% (-20 dB) of the maximum peak in the window (between 0 and 1). Short staccato plucks have low effective duration (~0.15), while ringing notes occupy a large fraction of the window. In this example, effective duration dynamically controls the decay time of an algorithmic stereo reverb: staccato notes get short snappy ambiences, while sustaining notes get lush lingering tails. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time effective duration.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("plucks.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic pluck fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(1.5);
            var env = EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.4), trig);
            Pluck.ar(WhiteNoise.ar * env, trig, 0.2, 1/220, 2.0, 0.3)
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var effDur = EffectiveDuration.kr(source, windowTime: 0.5, frameTime: 0.005);
        var durLag = effDur.lag(0.08);
        var revDecay = durLag.linexp(0.05, 0.8, 0.2, 2.5);
        var wet = CombC.ar(source, 0.5, [0.03, 0.045], revDecay) * 0.35;
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + wet;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, durLag.clip(0, 1)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Effective Duration", ~miraBus, 0.0, 1.0, "ratio");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
